{"name":"Changing Seasons","hex":"#b6927c","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"changing","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["present participle and gerund of change"]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Change; alteration."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/changing"},{"term":"seasons","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["plural of season"]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["third-person singular simple present indicative of season"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/seasons"}],"entries":[{"title":"Changing Seasons (music video)","blocks":[{"text":"Changing Seasons is a music video by Indian composer A. R. Rahman. The video was simultaneously released in Hindi and Tamil on 18 January 2011. The song \"Jaare Udd Jaare\" (Hindi) / \"Naan Varuvene\" (Tamil) featured in the video was composed by Rahman and performed by Rahman and Jali Fily Cissokho. The video, produced by Y. M. Movies and filmed by John Warner, features Aishwarya Rai along with Rahman. The song was originally composed for Bollywood film Raavan and its Tamil version Raavanan. The song was previously released on the Hindi Raavan and the Tamil Raavanan soundtrack albums respectively in 2010."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Changing_Seasons_(music_video)"},{"title":"Billy Bang","blocks":[{"text":"Billy Bang, born William Vincent Walker, was an American free jazz violinist and composer."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/49/Billy_Bang.png/330px-Billy_Bang.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Billy_Bang"},{"title":"Season","blocks":[{"text":"A season is a division of the year based on changes in weather, ecology, and the number of daylight hours in a given region. On Earth, seasons are the result of the axial parallelism of Earth's tilted orbit around the Sun. In temperate and polar regions, the seasons are marked by changes in the intensity of sunlight that reaches the Earth's surface, variations of which may cause animals to undergo hibernation or to migrate, and plants to be dormant. Various cultures define the number and nature of seasons based on regional variations, and as such there are a number of both modern and historical definitions of the seasons."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/91/ChangingSeasons_NH_01.png/330px-ChangingSeasons_NH_01.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Season"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9d/Billy_Bang.jpg/500px-Billy_Bang.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9d/Billy_Bang.jpg/500px-Billy_Bang.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Bang at Bach Dancing & Dynamite Society, Half Moon Bay CA 8/24/86, w/William Parker, bass; Oscar Sanders, guitar; Zen Matsuura, drums","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABilly_Bang.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b5/Vision_Festival.png/500px-Vision_Festival.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b5/Vision_Festival.png/1280px-Vision_Festival.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b5/Vision_Festival.png/500px-Vision_Festival.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"In 2008, with Fred Anderson, William Parker and Kidd Jordan","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AVision_Festival.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8b/North_season.jpg/500px-North_season.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, 